WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.665
Okay, so CLAUDE.md is Claude Code's instruction file,

2
00:00:03.665 --> 00:00:08.673
and AGENTS.md is the open format Codex reads for the same job.

3
00:00:08.673 --> 00:00:14.773
By default, Claude Code reads AGENTS.md only if there's no CLAUDE.md,

4
00:00:14.773 --> 00:00:16.353
so with both in a repo,

5
00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:18.812
each agent reads just its own file.

6
00:00:18.812 --> 00:00:22.727
So I keep AGENTS.md as the shared file,

7
00:00:22.727 --> 00:00:24.487
since more agents read it,

8
00:00:24.487 --> 00:00:29.898
and my CLAUDE.md starts with @AGENTS.md.

9
00:00:29.898 --> 00:00:32.578
Claude Code expands that import at launch,

10
00:00:32.578 --> 00:00:34.960
so one file serves both agents.

11
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.330
In that file,

12
00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:40.380
I write the commands and rules an agent can't infer from the code,

13
00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:42.780
and keep it under two hundred lines.
